Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 09:17:55 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 244/260] [ae-patch] Fix the review findings on the transcript
 keep: decide it by the server frontier

The first version kept the local Claude transcript when every toolu_ call id and the last
user text of the server items appeared in it. Review showed that accepts a file that
disagrees with the server: edited or retried turns, changed tool output, compaction, a
short last message that matches an earlier one, a chat with no tools.

The forwarder now records the server item count and last item id each time it moves its
cursor, next to the cursor's offset and fingerprint. A cold relaunch keeps the file only
when the cursor and that record still describe it, the server still holds exactly the
recorded frontier, the file ends cleanly and the image repair of a rebuild would change
nothing. The old forwarder is cancelled before its final cursor is read, and the cursor
and outcome travel in a context object instead of module state. Everything else rebuilds.
